## Required Sections (11) — use `##` headings

Microservices playbook posts use numbered `##` headings so section collapsibles group content cleanly.

1. **Executive Summary** — plain engineering language (2–4 sentences)
2. **Problem It Solves** — why naive approaches fail; symptom table
3. **Visual Architecture** — Mermaid `flowchart LR`, `stateDiagram-v2`, or `classDiagram`
4. **Core Flow** — Mermaid `sequenceDiagram` with `alt` branches (not numbered prose duplicating the diagram)
5. **Real-World Example** — ERP, fintech, BFSI, order-mgmt, payments, inventory scenarios
6. **Design Options / Patterns** — comparison tables (3+ options when applicable)
7. **Trade-offs** — Pros | Cons | When NOT to Use table
8. **Failure Scenarios** — production breakage table
9. **Best Practices** — operational guidance, resilience stack where relevant
10. **Interview Answer** — 60–90 second spoken blockquote
11. **Implementation** — all code inside `code-tabs` (Java / Go / Python / Pseudo)

Separate major sections with `---` horizontal rules.

---

## Code Snippets — Mandatory `code-tabs` Rule

**Every implementation code snippet belongs inside `code-tabs`.** Do not render languages as separate vertical sections.

### When to use `code-tabs`

| Content type | Use `code-tabs`? | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Java / Go / Python / Pseudo implementation | **Yes — required** | Under `## 11. Implementation` |
| Anti-pattern vs fixed example | **Yes** | All Java in `lang="java"` tab, etc. |
| Mermaid diagrams | **No** | Sections 3 and 4 |
| One-line inline `` `code` `` in prose | **No** | Fine in any section |
| Shell / YAML config snippets | **Optional** | Single fence in relevant tab or prose |

### Canonical template

```markdown
## 11. Implementation

{{< code-tabs default="java" java="Java" golang="Go" python="Python" pseudo="Pseudo" >}}
{{< code-tab lang="java" >}}

```java
// example
```

{{< /code-tab >}}
{{< code-tab lang="golang" >}}

```go
